<title>INDIA: India produced 2,656 tonnes lead in May.</title>
<headline>India produced 2,656 tonnes lead in May.</headline>
<dateline>NEW DELHI 1997-06-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>India produced 2,656 tonnes of lead in May against a target of 3,200 tonnes, a government statement said on Monday.</p>
<p>The country produced 5,892 tonnes of lead during April and May, compared with 6,036 tonnes in the same period in 1996, the</p>
<p>statement said.</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>	   Installed   May, 1997	 Cumulative output</p>
<p>	   capacity    ---------	 ------------------</p>
<p>	   (annual)	Actual	 Apr-May 97  Apr-May 96</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>HZL	 65,000	 1,515	    3,882	 3,341</p>
<p>ILL</p>
<p>Secondary 24,000	 1,141	    2,010	 2,695</p>
<p>- - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - - -</p>
<p>Total     89,000	 2,656	    5,892	 6,036</p>
<p>--------------------------------------------------------------</p>
<p>NOTE: Figures are in tonnes</p>
<p>-- New Delhi newsroom +91 11 301 2024</p>
